Content:
Note that your `rbind()` calls are incorrect since `table(c.dots)` and `table(w.dots)` do not count the same categories (e.g., in example 1, there is no case 6 in `c.dots`). You could do something like
`lvls <- sort(unique(c(c.dots, w.dots)));
cFac <- factor(c.dots, levels=lvls);
wFac <- factor(w.dots, levels=lvls)`
and then use `rbind(table(wFac), table(cFac))`.
